Keep the source NIC alive when duplicating discovery information fails.
Until FI_DUP succeeds, the shallow-copied NIC still belongs to the source.
Allocation and provider-copy failures must not close it during cleanup.

Based on ofiwg/libfabric v2.7.0.

--- a/src/fabric.c
+++ b/src/fabric.c
@@ -1661,6 +1661,8 @@
 	return dup;
 
 fail:
+	/* FI_DUP has not transferred ownership of a NIC to this copy. */
+	dup->nic = NULL;
 	fi_freeinfo(dup);
 	return NULL;
 }
